Subject: [PATCH 1/2] emacs: Make the notmuch archive key request an archive
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: nrmslrxmtsznwmlwpxkzspklzpoqrxos

notmuch-emacs's "a" key removes the inbox tag by default, which on
this list does nothing lasting: mail-tag.sh derives inbox from the
maildir and puts it back on the next notmuch new. Archiving a message
for good means moving its file under maildir/archive/, which just
archive does for every message tagged archive.

Adding archive makes "a" that request, so archiving is one key in
emacs followed by just archive. Removing inbox as well takes the
message out of the inbox at once, without waiting for the move.
---
change-id: nrmslrxmtsznwmlwpxkzspklzpoqrxos

 dotfiles/emacs/init.el | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dotfiles/emacs/init.el b/dotfiles/emacs/init.el
index e620223..c4f8426 100644
--- a/dotfiles/emacs/init.el
+++ b/dotfiles/emacs/init.el
@@ -576,6 +576,8 @@ and prefixes every line with \"> \"."
 (setq sendmail-program
       (expand-file-name "libexec/maildir-deliver.sh" user-emacs-directory))
 (setq notmuch-draft-tags '("+draft"))
+;; "a" asks just archive to move the message; it leaves the inbox now.
+(setq notmuch-archive-tags '("+archive" "-inbox"))
 (setq notmuch-search-oldest-first nil)
 (setq notmuch-show-only-matching-messages t)
 (setq notmuch-show-mark-read-tags nil)
